 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:15:18.114772Z",
 "text": "No, this clause is not enforceable. \n\nUnder the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a landlord is prohibited from charging or requiring a tenant to pay any fee, penalty, or extra charge unless it is specifically permitted by the Act or its regulations. While the regulations allow limited charges for NSF (bounced) cheques—capped at the landlord's actual bank charges plus a maximum $20 administrative fee—flat fees or penalties simply for paying rent late are not prescribed and are illegal (rendering the lease term void under section 4).\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 134",
